              "question": "<p>You can predict the actions of adrenaline on various organs, as the previous activity just proved. But the adrenergic alpha 2 receptor is a receptor primarily aimed at controlling the sympathetic nervous system response and does the opposite of what we would expect in some organs. Therefore, we will be putting the drugs that primarily act on the alpha 2 receptor aside and not discuss those drugs in this module. </p>\n"
